{"id":"56239458358186f6","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-invariant-measure.md","title":"Invariant Measure","display":"df-invariant-measure — Invariant Measure","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-invariant-measure","aliases":["58-df-invariant-measure"],"display":"df-invariant-measure — Invariant Measure","depends_on":["[[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-measurable-space.md]]","[[58-df-measurable-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-invariant-measure"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-invariant-measure</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-invariant-measure — Invariant Measure"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-measure.md\">../batch13/58-df-measure.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"7f96c502a4a99a46\" href=\"?note=7f96c502a4a99a46\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-measurable-space.md\">../batch09/58-df-measurable-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"bbbec05fde1d3b01\" href=\"?note=bbbec05fde1d3b01\" title=\"58-df-measurable-function\">58-df-measurable-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(X,\\Sigma)\">\\((X,\\Sigma)\\)</span> (measurable space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\in X^X\">\\(T\\in X^X\\)</span> (map candidate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu:\\Sigma\\to[0,\\infty]\">\\(\\mu:\\Sigma\\to[0,\\infty]\\)</span> (measure candidate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Measurable}_S(T;(X,\\Sigma),(X,\\Sigma))\">\\(\\operatorname{Measurable}_S(T;(X,\\Sigma),(X,\\Sigma))\\)</span> (measurability predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"bbbec05fde1d3b01\" href=\"?note=bbbec05fde1d3b01\" title=\"58-df-measurable-function\">58-df-measurable-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Measure}_S\\)</span> (measure predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-measure.md\">../batch13/58-df-measure.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S(\\mu,T;X,\\Sigma)\">\\(\\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S(\\mu,T;X,\\Sigma)\\)</span> (invariant-measure predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}invariant\\text{-}measure} \\vdash \\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S(\\mu,T;X,\\Sigma) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu,X,\\Sigma)\\land\\operatorname{Measurable}_S(T;(X,\\Sigma),(X,\\Sigma))\\land\\forall A\\in\\Sigma\\;(\\mu(T^{-1}[A])=\\mu(A))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}invariant\\text{-}measure} \\vdash \\mathrm{InvariantMeasure}_S(\\mu,T;X,\\Sigma) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu,X,\\Sigma)\\land\\operatorname{Measurable}_S(T;(X,\\Sigma),(X,\\Sigma))\\land\\forall A\\in\\Sigma\\;(\\mu(T^{-1}[A])=\\mu(A))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Invariant measures are fixed by pullback along the transformation.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch13/58-df-measure.md","status":"resolved","id":"ca832ed6bc22f728","anchor":"ref-1","target